  "body": "## Summary\n\nOwner finding (task-20260806-165917): the PM was still making manual AI queries every ten-minute cycle for two real reasons:\n\n1. **Re-deriving values that already exist in script output** — swap, `EMERGENCY_STOP`, worker count are already in Section 1 of `generate_pm_report_v3.py`. This is not a code gap; documented in the module docstring rather than \"fixed\" with new logic.\n2. **Two genuine gaps**: no PR merge-state tracking, no per-row status tracking for the PM's own recently-dispatched UMRs.\n\nThis PR closes gap 2 with two new deterministic, zero-AI-call sections (`SCRIPT_VERSION` 3.4.0 → 3.5.0):\n\n- **Section 16 — TRACKED PR MERGE STATE**: real `gh pr view` for every entry in a real, configurable, file-backed tracked-PR list (`TRACKED_PR_LIST_PATH`, env-overridable via `VERIDIAN_PM_REPORT_TRACKED_PR_LIST_PATH`, default `TRACKED_PRS.json`) — **never a hardcoded PR number in the script itself**. Ships with an empty list `[]`; no starter PRs were invented since the directive named none — PM/Owner populates it going forward.\n- **Section 17 — RECENT OWNER-DISPATCHED UMR STATUS**: real per-row listing of `umr_tasks` rows with `source_trigger='owner_dispatch_gateway'` from the trailing 2h (env-overridable via `VERIDIAN_PM_REPORT_OWNER_UMR_RECENT_WINDOW_HOURS`), complementing Section 14's aggregate-only counts with itemized detail.\n\n## SKILL.md disposition (honesty note)\n\nIndependently re-confirmed before writing anything: the real \"Reporting Contract V3\" SKILL.md remains inaccessible from this Linux server — it lives only at `C:\\Users\\Dell\\.claude\\scheduled-tasks\\veridian-server-sentinel\\SKILL.md` on the Owner's local Windows machine (per `UMR-20260806-091407-5767`'s own prior finding, re-verified via a bounded search across `/opt/veridian`: no SKILL.md, no synced copy, anywhere). The SPEC's final instruction (\"update SKILL.md to state plainly...\") could not be literally carried out from this server. The equivalent instruction was instead recorded in this script's own module docstring — the established practical substitute for SKILL.md here (same precedent as the earlier Section 4 placeholder-until-real-source situation) — with an explicit note for the Owner if a real synced copy of SKILL.md ever becomes reachable from this server.\n\n## Testing\n\n- 13 new unit tests (missing/malformed/wrong-shape config, real `gh pr view` success/failure via mocked `run_cmd`, end-to-end tracked-PR section, 2h-window correctness, empty-window honesty, missing-column graceful degrade).\n- Existing `test_end_to_end_smoke_run` and `test_render_report_text_survives_per_metric_insufficient_data` updated for the two new report keys/section headers.\n- Full suite: **115 passed, 1 pre-existing failure** (`test_end_to_end_smoke_run`, confirmed via `git stash` to fail identically on the base branch — a `load_module_from_path` monkeypatch gap for `gtm_test_script_build_check.py`, unrelated to Sections 16/17 and out of this PR's scope).\n- A standalone manual end-to-end run of `build_report()`/`render_report_text()` (full fake DB + fully-wired mocks) confirmed Sections 16-17 integrate correctly into the real pipeline.\n\nSee `PROGRESS.md` for full detail.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
